  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_1241",
    "context": "The phenomenon of cashless society has attracted people's attention, mainly due to the rapid development of mobile payment in recent years, covering people's clothing, food, housing and transportation, spreading to the corners of cities and towns, and making some people change the habit of using cash. Actively promoting the construction of a cashless society is of far-reaching significance: first, it will help to lower the threshold of financial services and better promote economic development; second, it will help to reduce and reduce the utilization rate and management costs of cash, and reduce the cost of issuing money. It will also accelerate the flow of funds. Third, it helps to establish an integrity system, identify, prevent and crack down on all kinds of illegal and criminal acts related to cash transactions, bribery and bribery, and effectively curb corruption.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, with regard to a cashless society, which of the following is not mentioned?",
    "options": [
      "A) Benefits for the financial industry",
      "B) The reason why it has attracted a lot of attention",
      "C) Relationship with currency issuance",
      "D) The impact on interpersonal relationships"
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nThe phenomenon of cashless society has attracted people's attention, mainly due to the rapid development of mobile payment in recent years, covering people's clothing, food, housing and transportation, spreading to the corners of cities and towns, and making some people change the habit of using cash. Actively promoting the construction of a cashless society is of far-reaching significance: first, it will help to lower the threshold of financial services and better promote economic development; second, it will help to reduce and reduce the utilization rate and management costs of cash, and reduce the cost of issuing money. It will also accelerate the flow of funds. Third, it helps to establish an integrity system, identify, prevent and crack down on all kinds of illegal and criminal acts related to cash transactions, bribery and bribery, and effectively curb corruption.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, with regard to a cashless society, which of the following is not mentioned?\n# Options:\nA) Benefits for the financial industry\nB) The reason why it has attracted a lot of attention\nC) Relationship with currency issuance\nD) The impact on interpersonal relationships\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option is not mentioned in the given context about a cashless society. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe context talks about how the cashless society has gained attention mainly because of the rapid development of mobile payments. These mobile payments have spread throughout cities and towns and have influenced people to change their cash usage habits. It mentions that promoting a cashless society has several benefits, including lowering the threshold of financial services, reducing the use and management costs of cash, and accelerating the flow of funds. Additionally, it helps in establishing an integrity system to prevent corruption by identifying and cracking down on illegal activities related to cash transactions and bribery.\n\nNow, looking at the question: it asks which of the options is NOT mentioned. The options are A to D.\n\nOption A: Benefits for the financial industry. The context does talk about benefits for financial services, like lowering the threshold and reducing costs, so this is mentioned.\n\nOption B: The reason why it has attracted attention. The context clearly states that it has attracted attention mainly due to mobile payment development, so this is mentioned.\n\nOption C: Relationship with currency issuance. The context mentions that cashless society helps reduce the use of cash and mentions the impact on financial services, including currency issuance. So this is also mentioned.\n\nOption D: The impact on interpersonal relationships. The context doesn't mention anything about how a cashless society affects people's relationships. It talks about economic and financial benefits, legal aspects, and fund flow, but nothing about interpersonal dynamics.\n\nSo, the one that's not mentioned is D.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": true
  },
  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_8698",
    "context": "A class plans to select two from three girls, including Fang Rufen, Guo Yanran, and He Zhilian, and three from five boys, including Peng Youwen, Qiu Zhijie, Ren Xiangyang, Song Wenkai, and Tang Xiaohua, to form a group of five college students to teach on a voluntary basis in the mountain area. Requirements: (1) Guo Yanran and Tang Xiaohua are not selected at the same time; (2) Peng Youwen and Song Wenkai are not selected at the same time; (3) Qiu Zhijie and Tang Xiaohua are not selected at the same time.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, if Tang Xiaohua is selected, which of the following two must be selected?",
    "options": [
      "A) Fang rufen and guo yanran",
      "B) Guo yanran and he zhilian",
      "C) Peng youwen and he zhilian",
      "D) Fang rufen and he zhilian"
