  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_14171",
    "context": "Insurance agent: Cars are no safer than motorcycles; that is, when driven at high speeds, cars are not involved in more fatal crashes than are motorcycles. We conducted a survey about car Y and found that highspeed crashes involving car Y resulted in 40% of the fatalities in 2005 while motorcycles were involved in only 35% of the fatalities in 2005.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, each of the following describes a potential flaw in the insurance agent's reasoning EXCEPT:",
    "options": [
      "A) A conclusion is drawn about cars in general on the basis of a study focusing on car y.",
      "B) The survey being used to support the conclusion failed to take into account the significance of the total number of motorcycles that are driven compared to the numbers of car y that are driven.",
      "C) The safety of a vehicle might depend on other factors besides how often that vehicle is involved in high-speed crashes resulting in fatalities.",
      "D) The insurance agent based his conclusion on the total number of car crashes, not just on those resulting in fatalities."
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nInsurance agent: Cars are no safer than motorcycles; that is, when driven at high speeds, cars are not involved in more fatal crashes than are motorcycles. We conducted a survey about car Y and found that highspeed crashes involving car Y resulted in 40% of the fatalities in 2005 while motorcycles were involved in only 35% of the fatalities in 2005.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, each of the following describes a potential flaw in the insurance agent's reasoning EXCEPT:\n# Options:\nA) A conclusion is drawn about cars in general on the basis of a study focusing on car y.\nB) The survey being used to support the conclusion failed to take into account the significance of the total number of motorcycles that are driven compared to the numbers of car y that are driven.\nC) The safety of a vehicle might depend on other factors besides how often that vehicle is involved in high-speed crashes resulting in fatalities.\nD) The insurance agent based his conclusion on the total number of car crashes, not just on those resulting in fatalities.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
