  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_11798",
    "context": "By examining fossilized beetles, a research team has produced the most detailed description yet of temperatures in Britain over the past 22, 000 years. Fossils of species that still exist were selected and dated. When individuals of several species found in the same place were found to date to the same period, the known temperature tolerances of the existing beetle species were used to determine the maximum summer temperature that could have existed at that place and period.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, the procedure of the researchers assumes which one of the following?",
    "options": [
      "A) The temperature tolerances of the beetle species did not change significantly during the 22, 000-year period.",
      "B) Beetles can tolerate warm weather better than cold weather.",
      "C) The process of dating is more accurate for beetles than for other organisms.",
      "D) Fossils of different species found in the same place belonged to different period."
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nBy examining fossilized beetles, a research team has produced the most detailed description yet of temperatures in Britain over the past 22, 000 years. Fossils of species that still exist were selected and dated. When individuals of several species found in the same place were found to date to the same period, the known temperature tolerances of the existing beetle species were used to determine the maximum summer temperature that could have existed at that place and period.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the procedure of the researchers assumes which one of the following?\n# Options:\nA) The temperature tolerances of the beetle species did not change significantly during the 22, 000-year period.\nB) Beetles can tolerate warm weather better than cold weather.\nC) The process of dating is more accurate for beetles than for other organisms.\nD) Fossils of different species found in the same place belonged to different period.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the answer to this question about Pancake Man based on the given context. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about \"Pancake people,\" who are described as intellectuals but with a different approach. Instead of focusing deeply on a particular area, they have a broad knowledge base but not in-depth expertise. They love money reading, which I think refers to consuming a lot of information, possibly through search engines. They don't really think critically or use their imagination much. Their \"noodles\" are as big as pancakes, which is a metaphor for their knowledge being broad but not necessarily deep. They can quickly obtain scarce information, especially the positive aspects, but this makes them reluctant to dive deep into any subject.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A to D is true about Pancake Man. Let's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Be good at learning new knowledge. The context says they have a basic knowledge in various fields but aren't proficient in any particular area. So, they might not be great at learning new knowledge deeply, but they can learn a bit about many things. I'm not sure if this is the best fit.\n\nOption B: Ability to learn by analogy. The context doesn't mention anything about learning through analogy. It talks more about their broad but shallow knowledge and their reluctance to delve into a subject deeply. So, I don't think this is correct.\n\nOption C: Keen to cover a wide range, but does not require a good explanation. The context does say they have a love for money reading, implying a wide range of knowledge, and they don't require a good explanation because they don't think deeply. This seems to align with the description.\n\nOption D: Occupy a large number of scarce information resources. The context mentions that they can obtain scarce information quickly, especially the positive side, but it doesn't say they occupy a lot of resources. Instead, it's more about the ease of access rather than occupying resources.\n\nPutting it all together, Option C seems to fit best because it captures both their broad knowledge and their lack of deep understanding or critical thinking.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_11543",
    "context": "Editorial: Our society has a vested interest in maintaining a political system in which candidates are free to adhere to their principles. Yet campaigning for elected office is extremely costly, and because only the wealthiest individuals are able to finance their own political campaigns, most candidates must seek funding from private sources. In so doing, the candidates are almost invariably obliged to compromise their principles. Thus, government itself should assume the cost of candidates' campaigns.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which one of the following principles, if valid, most helps to justify the conclusion as it is drawn in the argument?",
    "options": [
      "A) Candidates should not run for elected office if doing so would compel the candidates to compromise their principles.",
      "B) Voters should not support a candidate if that candidate is known to have accepted funding from private sources.",
      "C) Candidates wealthy enough to finance their own political campaigns should not be permitted to raise additional funds from private sources.",
      "D) The government should finance a given activity if doing so will further a vested interest of society."
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nEditorial: Our society has a vested interest in maintaining a political system in which candidates are free to adhere to their principles. Yet campaigning for elected office is extremely costly, and because only the wealthiest individuals are able to finance their own political campaigns, most candidates must seek funding from private sources. In so doing, the candidates are almost invariably obliged to compromise their principles. Thus, government itself should assume the cost of candidates' campaigns.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following principles, if valid, most helps to justify the conclusion as it is drawn in the argument?\n# Options:\nA) Candidates should not run for elected office if doing so would compel the candidates to compromise their principles.\nB) Voters should not support a candidate if that candidate is known to have accepted funding from private sources.\nC) Candidates wealthy enough to finance their own political campaigns should not be permitted to raise additional funds from private sources.\nD) The government should finance a given activity if doing so will further a vested interest of society.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the answer to this question about Pancake Man based on the given context. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about \"Pancake people,\" who are described as intellectuals but with a different approach. Instead of focusing deeply on a particular area, they have a broad knowledge base but not in-depth expertise. They love money reading, which I think refers to consuming a lot of information, possibly through search engines. They don't really think critically or use their imagination much. Their \"noodles\" are as big as pancakes, which is a metaphor for their knowledge being broad but not necessarily deep. They can quickly obtain scarce information, especially the positive aspects, but this makes them reluctant to dive deep into any subject.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A to D is true about Pancake Man. Let's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Be good at learning new knowledge. The context says they have a basic knowledge in various fields but aren't proficient in any particular area. So, they might not be great at learning new knowledge deeply, but they can learn a bit about many things. I'm not sure if this is the best fit.\n\nOption B: Ability to learn by analogy. The context doesn't mention anything about learning through analogy. It talks more about their broad but shallow knowledge and their reluctance to delve into a subject deeply. So, I don't think this is correct.\n\nOption C: Keen to cover a wide range, but does not require a good explanation. The context does say they have a love for money reading, implying a wide range of knowledge, and they don't require a good explanation because they don't think deeply. This seems to align with the description.\n\nOption D: Occupy a large number of scarce information resources. The context mentions that they can obtain scarce information quickly, especially the positive side, but it doesn't say they occupy a lot of resources. Instead, it's more about the ease of access rather than occupying resources.\n\nPutting it all together, Option C seems to fit best because it captures both their broad knowledge and their lack of deep understanding or critical thinking.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
