  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_14970",
    "context": "Consumer magazine: Because front-loading washers use less water than top-loading washers, ordinary powder detergent does not dissolve readily in front-loading washers. So, to get clothes really clean in a front-loading machine you need to use a detergent formulated especially for front-loading washers, instead of ordinary powder detergent.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which one of the following is an assumption required by the argument in the consumer magazine?",
    "options": [
      "A) A laundry detergent does not get clothes really clean in a washer unless it dissolves readily in it.",
      "B) A washing machine gets clothes really clean only with a laundry detergent specially formulated for that machine.",
      "C) A laundry detergent formulated especially for front-loading washers dissolves more readily in them than it does in top-loading washers.",
      "D) Washers that use more water get clothes cleaner than those that use less."
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nConsumer magazine: Because front-loading washers use less water than top-loading washers, ordinary powder detergent does not dissolve readily in front-loading washers. So, to get clothes really clean in a front-loading machine you need to use a detergent formulated especially for front-loading washers, instead of ordinary powder detergent.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is an assumption required by the argument in the consumer magazine?\n# Options:\nA) A laundry detergent does not get clothes really clean in a washer unless it dissolves readily in it.\nB) A washing machine gets clothes really clean only with a laundry detergent specially formulated for that machine.\nC) A laundry detergent formulated especially for front-loading washers dissolves more readily in them than it does in top-loading washers.\nD) Washers that use more water get clothes cleaner than those that use less.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the answer to this question about Pancake Man based on the given context. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about \"Pancake people,\" who are described as intellectuals but with a different approach. Instead of focusing deeply on a particular area, they have a broad knowledge base but not in-depth expertise. They love money reading, which I think refers to consuming a lot of information, possibly through search engines. They don't really think critically or use their imagination much. Their \"noodles\" are as big as pancakes, which is a metaphor for their knowledge being broad but not necessarily deep. They can quickly obtain scarce information, especially the positive aspects, but this makes them reluctant to dive deep into any subject.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A to D is true about Pancake Man. Let's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Be good at learning new knowledge. The context says they have a basic knowledge in various fields but aren't proficient in any particular area. So, they might not be great at learning new knowledge deeply, but they can learn a bit about many things. I'm not sure if this is the best fit.\n\nOption B: Ability to learn by analogy. The context doesn't mention anything about learning through analogy. It talks more about their broad but shallow knowledge and their reluctance to delve into a subject deeply. So, I don't think this is correct.\n\nOption C: Keen to cover a wide range, but does not require a good explanation. The context does say they have a love for money reading, implying a wide range of knowledge, and they don't require a good explanation because they don't think deeply. This seems to align with the description.\n\nOption D: Occupy a large number of scarce information resources. The context mentions that they can obtain scarce information quickly, especially the positive side, but it doesn't say they occupy a lot of resources. Instead, it's more about the ease of access rather than occupying resources.\n\nPutting it all together, Option C seems to fit best because it captures both their broad knowledge and their lack of deep understanding or critical thinking.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_9085",
    "context": "Most plants produce chemicals that resist parasites in the process of long-term evolution. Plants commonly used by humans contain about 40 natural drugs, that is, complex chemical toxins against bacteria, fungi and other parasites. People ingest these toxins every day without poisoning, so the new harm caused by synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops is very small.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, if the following statement is true, which of the followings does not undermine the above argument?",
    "options": [
      "A) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than that of synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops",
      "B) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them",
      "C) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually simpler than that of natural drugs contained in plants",
      "D) Natural drugs contained in plants are usually only suitable for resisting specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides are usually harmful to a variety of organisms"
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nMost plants produce chemicals that resist parasites in the process of long-term evolution. Plants commonly used by humans contain about 40 natural drugs, that is, complex chemical toxins against bacteria, fungi and other parasites. People ingest these toxins every day without poisoning, so the new harm caused by synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops is very small.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the following statement is true, which of the followings does not undermine the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than that of synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops\nB) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them\nC) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually simpler than that of natural drugs contained in plants\nD) Natural drugs contained in plants are usually only suitable for resisting specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides are usually harmful to a variety of organisms\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
