    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_6332",
    "context": "In Sweden, known as the model of a high-welfare country, the benefits of non-working people are almost the same as their wages, and they do not have to pay taxes. Generous sick pay means that workers can get 90% of their wages even if they are sick. Although the Swedes are the healthiest citizens in Europe, the average annual sick leave for employees is no less than 50 days, accounting for almost one-fifth of the working time of the year.",
