      "D) The power of traditional culture forced buddhism to adopt flexible strategies in its dissemination"
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nUnder the severe impact of Chinese culture, Buddhism cannot gain a foothold in China if it cannot adapt to the reality, so Buddhism can only make some camouflage in order to survive.Among the typical examples of early Buddhism, some especially emphasize that the word filial piety distorts the meaning of the original text in order to meet the requirements of China's strong color culture.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the most appropriate summary of the main idea of the passage?\n# Options:\nA) Buddhism is a very adaptable religion\nB) Filial piety is one of the important meanings derived from the development of buddhist scriptures\nC) Buddhism has a deep influence on the inheritance of chinese traditional culture\nD) The power of traditional culture forced buddhism to adopt flexible strategies in its dissemination\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
