  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_11653",
    "context": "The crux of creativity resides in the ability to manufacture variation on a theme. If we look at the history of science, for instance, we see that every idea is built upon a thousand related ideas. Careful analysis leads us to understand that what we choose to call a new theme or a new discovery is itself always and without exception some sort of variation, on a deep level, of previous themes.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, if all of the statements in the passage are true, each of the following must also be true EXCEPT:",
    "options": [
      "A) All great scientific discoverers have been able to manufacture a variation on a theme.",
      "B) Careful analysis of a specific variation can reveal previous themes of which it is a variation.",
      "C) Some new scientific discoveries do not represent, on a deep level, a variation on previous themes.",
      "D) No scientific idea is entirely independent of all other ideas."
    ],
    "answer": "C",
