  },
  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_2127",
    "context": "In general, young children's body temperature rises less as a result of sun exposure than adults'. However, it has been found that heat stroke is more likely to occur in young children if the temperature is high in a car compartment, and almost infrequently in adults. You won't get sunstroke even if you stay in a car for an hour at 45 degree. Which of the following, if true, best explains these findings?",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which of the following, if true, best explains these findings?",
    "options": [
      "A) Among children 0 to 3 years old, the younger the child, the less resistance",
      "B) As people age, the proportion of water in their body fluids decreases, and their temperature changes less dramatically",
      "C) The car belongs to a confined space, when the outdoor temperature reaches, the car temperature can be reached, and adults in the car is likely to open the window when they feel uncomfortable",
      "D) Heat stroke usually occurs when you lose your body weight in water. young children have a larger body surface area to absorb heat more quickly, and because they have the same number of sweat glands as adults, they lose water more quickly"
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nIn general, young children's body temperature rises less as a result of sun exposure than adults'. However, it has been found that heat stroke is more likely to occur in young children if the temperature is high in a car compartment, and almost infrequently in adults. You won't get sunstroke even if you stay in a car for an hour at 45 degree. Which of the following, if true, best explains these findings?\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best explains these findings?\n# Options:\nA) Among children 0 to 3 years old, the younger the child, the less resistance\nB) As people age, the proportion of water in their body fluids decreases, and their temperature changes less dramatically\nC) The car belongs to a confined space, when the outdoor temperature reaches, the car temperature can be reached, and adults in the car is likely to open the window when they feel uncomfortable\nD) Heat stroke usually occurs when you lose your body weight in water. young children have a larger body surface area to absorb heat more quickly, and because they have the same number of sweat glands as adults, they lose water more quickly\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
