  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_1422",
    "context": "The cultural industry integrates intensive talent, technology, knowledge and capital, and has distinct cross-disciplinary, cross-disciplinary, cross-time-space and cross-cultural characteristics. It will also play a central role in future personal behavior, social life and nation-building, as well as global development and human affairs. Report of the World Commission on Culture and Development of the United Nations Scientific, Educational and Cultural Organization in 1995. It is pointed out that culture is the ultimate goal and destination of the overall prosperity and development of human existence. It can be said that the cross-border characteristics and importance of culture put forward fundamental requirements for the high quality and scale of cultural talents.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which of the following is the main content of this text?",
    "options": [
      "A) Cultural industry plays an important role in human social life",
      "B) Cultural talents should have high quality and scale",
      "C) Culture is the ultimate goal of human prosperity and development",
      "D) The particularity and importance of cultural industry"
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nThe cultural industry integrates intensive talent, technology, knowledge and capital, and has distinct cross-disciplinary, cross-disciplinary, cross-time-space and cross-cultural characteristics. It will also play a central role in future personal behavior, social life and nation-building, as well as global development and human affairs. Report of the World Commission on Culture and Development of the United Nations Scientific, Educational and Cultural Organization in 1995. It is pointed out that culture is the ultimate goal and destination of the overall prosperity and development of human existence. It can be said that the cross-border characteristics and importance of culture put forward fundamental requirements for the high quality and scale of cultural talents.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Cultural industry plays an important role in human social life\nB) Cultural talents should have high quality and scale\nC) Culture is the ultimate goal of human prosperity and development\nD) The particularity and importance of cultural industry\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_thinking": "\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the answer to this question about Pancake Man based on the given context. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it correctly.\n\nThe context talks about \"Pancake people,\" who are described as intellectuals but with a different approach. Instead of focusing deeply on a particular area, they have a broad knowledge base but not in-depth expertise. They love money reading, which I think refers to consuming a lot of information, possibly through search engines. They don't really think critically or use their imagination much. Their \"noodles\" are as big as pancakes, which is a metaphor for their knowledge being broad but not necessarily deep. They can quickly obtain scarce information, especially the positive aspects, but this makes them reluctant to dive deep into any subject.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A to D is true about Pancake Man. Let's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Be good at learning new knowledge. The context says they have a basic knowledge in various fields but aren't proficient in any particular area. So, they might not be great at learning new knowledge deeply, but they can learn a bit about many things. I'm not sure if this is the best fit.\n\nOption B: Ability to learn by analogy. The context doesn't mention anything about learning through analogy. It talks more about their broad but shallow knowledge and their reluctance to delve into a subject deeply. So, I don't think this is correct.\n\nOption C: Keen to cover a wide range, but does not require a good explanation. The context does say they have a love for money reading, implying a wide range of knowledge, and they don't require a good explanation because they don't think deeply. This seems to align with the description.\n\nOption D: Occupy a large number of scarce information resources. The context mentions that they can obtain scarce information quickly, especially the positive side, but it doesn't say they occupy a lot of resources. Instead, it's more about the ease of access rather than occupying resources.\n\nPutting it all together, Option C seems to fit best because it captures both their broad knowledge and their lack of deep understanding or critical thinking.\n",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_answer": "",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_result": false
  },
  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_12617",
    "context": "With a record number of new companies starting up in Derderia, and with previously established companies adding many new jobs, a record number of new jobs were created last year in the Derderian economy. This year, previously established companies will not be adding as many new jobs overall as such companies added last year. Ttherefore, unless a record number of companies start up this year, Derderia will not break its record for new jobs created.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which of the following is an assumption on which the argument relies?",
    "options": [
      "A) This year, the new companies starting up will not provide substantially more jobs per company than did new companies last year.",
      "B) The number of people seeking employment is no larger this year than it was last year.",
      "C) In a given year, new companies starting up create more new jobs on average than do previously established companies.",
      "D) The number of jobs created in the derderian economy last year was substantially larger than the number of jobs lost."
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nWith a record number of new companies starting up in Derderia, and with previously established companies adding many new jobs, a record number of new jobs were created last year in the Derderian economy. This year, previously established companies will not be adding as many new jobs overall as such companies added last year. Ttherefore, unless a record number of companies start up this year, Derderia will not break its record for new jobs created.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is an assumption on which the argument relies?\n# Options:\nA) This year, the new companies starting up will not provide substantially more jobs per company than did new companies last year.\nB) The number of people seeking employment is no larger this year than it was last year.\nC) In a given year, new companies starting up create more new jobs on average than do previously established companies.\nD) The number of jobs created in the derderian economy last year was substantially larger than the number of jobs lost.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
