  {
    "id": "LOGIQA_dev_6300",
    "context": "The apples on a tree are ripe. Because the tree is too high to reach on tiptoe, I had to move to the wooden ladder. Just as I reached out to pick it, the apple suddenly fell down and fell to the ground, becoming a ball of fruit mud. That is the so-called helplessness in life. I saw it dropping, but I missed it. But it was not in vain. At least, I knew that that apple didn't belong to me. If I come down from the wooden ladder at that time, it's not too late to pick from other trees.",
    "question": "Based on the above information, which one of the followings is the most important enlightenment from this story?",
    "options": [
      "A) In reality, we should be good at discovering and seizing opportunities.",
      "B) In life, we should not be discouraged or lose ourselves, and we should keep trying and pursuing.",
      "C) When we encounter anything, we should keep an ordinary heart and learn to be calm.",
      "D) Any exploration in life is the accumulation of successful experience."
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_input": "Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format \"\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D\".\n####\n# Context:\nThe apples on a tree are ripe. Because the tree is too high to reach on tiptoe, I had to move to the wooden ladder. Just as I reached out to pick it, the apple suddenly fell down and fell to the ground, becoming a ball of fruit mud. That is the so-called helplessness in life. I saw it dropping, but I missed it. But it was not in vain. At least, I knew that that apple didn't belong to me. If I come down from the wooden ladder at that time, it's not too late to pick from other trees.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the followings is the most important enlightenment from this story?\n# Options:\nA) In reality, we should be good at discovering and seizing opportunities.\nB) In life, we should not be discouraged or lose ourselves, and we should keep trying and pursuing.\nC) When we encounter anything, we should keep an ordinary heart and learn to be calm.\nD) Any exploration in life is the accumulation of successful experience.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:",
    "cot0shot.math teacher_output": "\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning is that Pancake Man is described as having a broad knowledge base but not requiring a deep explanation, which aligns with Option C.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
